WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.050
Heat and flooding shape cold storage decisions.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.050
This is GEONOS.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:11.100
Compare two buildings, inspect the evidence, and plan your next site visit.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:17.770
Speak a building question; Muse Voice turns it into an editable message.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:23.690
Select two New York buildings and ask which checks matter for a climate-resilient retrofit.

00:00:25.155 --> 00:00:30.085
Spark retrieves official records and follows your question into climate evidence.

00:00:30.115 --> 00:00:32.855
These scenarios use the same rainfall.

00:00:32.915 --> 00:00:41.975
In the 2050 map, the deep-water class touches 572 Smith’s outline; it is about forty-seven meters from 592.

00:00:43.447 --> 00:00:51.177
That contrast directs the next visit: locate entrances, loading access, and essential equipment, then check

00:00:51.207 --> 00:00:52.697
their elevations.

00:00:52.727 --> 00:00:55.227
Your requirements stay explicit.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:01:01.627
A twenty-thousand-square-foot footprint condition supports one candidate and conflicts with the other.

00:01:03.113 --> 00:01:08.973
SAM 3.1 marks roof and tree regions on actual 2024 aerial images.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:14.283
Wonder reviews the structured detections with public records and recommends the next survey.

00:01:14.313 --> 00:01:17.533
Open the evidence to see where each question came from.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:25.320
DINOv2 runs locally, comparing 2020 and 2024 visual features.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.010
Drag across the original photographs to inspect the highlighted locations.

00:01:31.488 --> 00:01:35.778
Bring a planning note into Muse Glimmer, running on this computer.

00:01:35.808 --> 00:01:43.138
It connects your requirement to quoted records, proposes the first owner request, and explains which measured

00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:46.018
finding could change the next inspection.

00:01:46.048 --> 00:01:48.228
Notes stay local.

00:01:49.697 --> 00:01:54.197
Muse Image turns written checks into an illustrated inspection plan.

00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:59.717
This earlier example connects each action to the decision it could change.

00:02:00.017 --> 00:02:03.877
Open its written checks alongside the generated concept.

00:02:05.363 --> 00:02:13.413
Built during this hackathon, GEONOS connects over a million valid mapped footprints, existing public datasets,

00:02:13.443 --> 00:02:18.743
and pretrained Meta models through one focused map and conversation.

00:02:20.238 --> 00:02:27.408
Station weather, regional projections, energy reports, and citywide geometry give each question a source and

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:28.418
scale.

00:02:28.638 --> 00:02:34.848
Seven Meta model roles connect a spoken question to evidence, an inspection, and a better-informed building

00:02:34.878 --> 00:02:35.858
decision.
